{
 "id": "bigville_fisc_church",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "BIGVILLE R9 (block 257000) -- the CHURCH, the THIRD (voluntary, NO-lever) institution funded by DONATION. fc_tithe: a TITHER gives a COMMITTED FRACTION of income (tithe_due = IDiv(income*tithe_bp+5000, 10000), INTEGER coin -- the cross-frame fraction INTENSIONAL, the invariant shared with interest/tax). fc_donate_occasional: DISJOINT (tithe_bp=0) discretionary giving WHEN FLUSH; devotion=none matches NEITHER -> income 0 (ablate devotion -> 0). fc_stipend pays Mary FROM funds iff donations sufficed (fc_stipend_unfunded marks her UNPAID otherwise -- precarity, NO lever). fc_charity redistributes to the poor (fc_charity_unfunded: the plate is empty in a downturn -> charity FAILS when most needed -- procyclical). fc_church_defunct + fc_parsonage_precarious: a defunct church costs Mary the stipend AND the TIED parsonage. fc_counsel is CO-REGULATION (reuse the 239000 safety channel): a distressed resident approaching a SAFE Mary returns toward the window (arousal down / valence up); a dysregulated counsellor (safe=0) -> no return (the 239 control). Composes existing Terms; zero new Rust; self_load_only.",
